.1768776626919965,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":-0.0797091997955761,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.18237274365247305,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.1439544094903733,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":97.0,"_gate_margins":0.005979030027571747,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":56.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04503714142585975,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":61.2,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012426660326295988,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":79.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.0032,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Viatris Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a healthcare company in North America, Europe, China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Japan, Australia, New Zealand, rest of Asia, Africa, Latin America, and the Middle East. It operates in four segments: Developed Markets, Greater China, JANZ, and Emerging Markets. The company offers prescription brand drugs, generic drugs, complex generic drugs, and biosimilars. It also provides drugs in various therapeutic areas covering various noncommunicable and infectious diseases, including cardiovascular, CNS and anesthesia, dermatology, diabetes and metabolism, eye care, gastroenterology, immunology, oncology, and respiratory and allergy, as well as support services, such as diagnostic clinics, educational seminars, and digital tools to help patients better manage their health. In addition, the company offers medicines in the form of oral solid doses, injectables, and complex dosage forms to retail and pharmacy establishments, wholesalers and distributors, payers, insurers and governments, and institutions. It distributes its products through pharmaceutical wholesalers/distributors, pharmaceutical retailers, institutional pharmacies, mail-order and e-commerce pharmacies, and specialty pharmacies under the Lyrica, Lipitor, Celebrex, Viagra, Creon, Influvac, Wixela Inhub, EpiPen Auto-Injector, Fraxiparine, Yupelri, Norvasc, Amitiza, Effexor, Lipacreon, Zoloft, Xalabrands, Dymista, Xanax, and Breyna brands. The company has collaboration agreements with Mapi Pharma Ltd. to develop and commercialize long-acting glatiramer acetate depot products and additional products; Revance Therapeutics, Inc. to develop, manufacture, and commercialize a biosimilar to the branded biologic product, BOTOX; and Theravance Biopharma, Inc. to develop and commercialize revefenacin. Viatris Inc. was founded in 1961 and is headquartered in Canonsburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott Andrew Smith Ph.D. | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $5.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 30K people. Revenue per employee of $477K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $65K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Viatris Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $23.9B market cap on $14.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -3.4pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The business throws off $1.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 96.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -5.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.4pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 960% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7707390648567127},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 48% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Did Raised Guidance Just Shift Viatris (VTRS) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-vtrs/viatris/news/did-raised-guidance-just-shift-viatris-vtrs-investment-narra","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794507733.313,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Is Viatris (NASDAQ:VTRS) Lifting Its Guidance?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/value/is-viatris-nasdaqvtrs-lifting-its-guidance","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794385860.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"VTRS or DHR: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027511/vtrs-or-dhr-which-is-the-better-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3027511","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794339490.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Viatris Named to Fortune's World's Best Workplaces